### System Prompt: Multimodal Meme Detection Architecture

**Context & Project Goal:**
We are developing a high-utility, impressive final-year college project: an intent-driven, multimodal meme detection system designed to catch offensive and hateful memes. The core goal is to look beyond literal translations of text and images to capture the *holistic intent* of the meme. The system is built using the **PyTorch** deep learning framework, relies heavily on **pre-trained Hugging Face transformers**, and is optimized to run efficiently within a budget-friendly cloud environment (**Google Colab with a single T4 GPU**). 

**The Core Gaps We Are Fixing (Where Other Repositories Fail):** 

1. **Late Fusion Disconnection:** Most open-source projects rely on late-fusion vector concatenation (torch.cat), treating text and images in silos and failing to detect sarcasm/irony. We are building a mid-fusion cross-attention mechanism.
2. **Loss of Spatial/Layout Context:** Standard projects extract raw OCR text strings but strip away structural context. We are mapping bounding box spatial coordinates directly into the text embedding space.
3. **Lack of Cultural Subtext:** Standard models interpret images literally. We use a frozen, local Visual Language Model (VLM) to pre-extract template subtext and cultural meaning without relying on expensive external APIs.

