### Detailed Technical Component Stack

1. **Preprocessing & Feature Augmentation Layer:** 

  * **EasyOCR Engine:** Extracts text tokens alongside 4D spatial coordinate matrices (xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax). These coordinates pass through a trainable nn.Linear mapping layer to match the hidden dimensions of the text tokens, allowing layout-aware injection.
  * **Frozen VLM (Salesforce/blip2-opt-2.7b):** Runs local, fast zero-shot inference on the T4 GPU via Hugging Face. It answers the prompt: *"What is the emotional context or template meaning of this meme?"*. The output text string is appended to the OCR text to enrich it with explicit cultural context before tokenization.
2. **Dual-Encoder Foundation Layer:** 

  * **Text Encoder:** Pre-trained Hugging Face CLIPTextModel. Base weights remain frozen to maximize T4 memory efficiency. It ingests the combined OCR text, VLM context text, and spatial layout embeddings.
  * **Vision Encoder:** Pre-trained Hugging Face CLIPVisionModel. Base weights remain frozen. It extracts granular visual patch embeddings from the meme image.
3. **Trainable Fusion & Head Layer (Our Core Code Contribution):** 

  * **Cross-Attention Multi-Head Layer:** A custom-written PyTorch block where text embeddings act as Queries (Q) interacting with visual Keys (K) and Values (V), and vice-versa. This dynamically calculates cross-modal interaction matrices.
  * **MLP Classification Head:** A small, fully connected classification network stacked with Dropout layers to prevent overfitting. This layer outputs the final classification mapping for offensive meme categorization.

**Target Benchmarks & Datasets:**
The pipeline will be trained and evaluated using benchmark datasets specifically rich in multi-modal intent, starting with the **Facebook Hateful Memes Dataset (Phase 2)** and **MAMI (Multimedia Automatic Misogyny Identification)**. 

