1. Introduction

1.1 Purpose

The purpose of this project is to design and develop an intelligent multimodal AI system capable of detecting potentially harmful memes by jointly analyzing textual and visual information. The system aims to assist content moderation by identifying harmful memes while minimizing false positives through confidence-based decision making.

Rather than replacing human moderators, the system will function as an AI-assisted moderation tool capable of automatically handling high-confidence cases and escalating uncertain cases for human review.

⸻

1.2 Problem Statement

The rapid growth of social media has led to an increase in harmful memes that spread hate speech, harassment, misinformation, and abusive content.

Traditional text-only or image-only moderation systems often fail because the harmful intent usually emerges only from the combination of image and text.

Additionally, cultural references, sarcasm, dark humor, and multilingual content make automated moderation significantly more challenging.

